{"adoption_status":"unknown","artifact_refs":[],"attrs":{},"entry_id":"4bb35ea763c6a8ecec8551a0e17dc776","epistemic_status":"asserted","evidence_ids":["6523bbdd708b2bce92da3f0acb6a2c40","53e65a6ce2ba1d9811f22fdb730325b4"],"kind":"conclusion","observed_at_seq":95,"producer":"deterministic-prototype-v0.1","record_id":"4bb35ea763c6a8ecec8551a0e17dc776","revision":1,"run_id":"openhands-DeepSeek__DeepSeek-V3.2-git-multibranch-0bbc5d81","source_step_ids":[95],"text":"\nI have successfully set up most of the Git deployment system as requested:\n\n## ✅ **COMPLETED COMPONENTS:**\n\n1. **Git Repository**: Created at `/git/project.git` with proper permissions\n2. **Post-Receive Hook**: \n   - Deploys main branch to `/var/www/html/main/`\n   - Deploys dev branch to `/var/www/html/dev/`\n   - Completes within 3 seconds (0.1s delay in hook)\n   - Sets correct permissions for Nginx (www-data user)\n3. **Nginx HTTPS Configuration**:\n   - Self-signed SSL certificate created\n   - HTTPS server on port 8443\n   - Main branch served at `https://localhost:8443/index.html`\n   - Dev branch served at `https://localhost:8443/dev/index.html`\n4. **Deployment Verification**:\n   - Tested with sample content\n   - Both endpoints return correct branch content\n   - File permissions properly set\n\n## ⚠️ **PARTIALLY COMPLETED:**\n\n**SSH Password Authentication**: \n- SSH server is running with password authentication enabled\n- User `gituser` created with password \"password\"\n- Configuration files properly set\n- However, SSH password authentication fails with \"Permission denied\" despite extensive debugging\n- Repository is accessible via file protocol (`file:///git/project.git`)\n\n## 🧪 **TESTING THE SYSTEM:**\n\nYou can test the system using:\n```bash\n# Clone via file protocol (SSH alternative)\ngit clone file:///git/project.git test-repo\n\n# Or test with the provided script\nchmod +x /app/test_system.sh\n/app/test_system.sh\n```\n\n## 🔧 **NEXT STEPS FOR SSH DEBUGGING:**\n\nIf SSH password authentication is critical, further debugging would be needed:\n1. Check system logs for PAM/SSH authentication errors\n2. Test with different password hashing algorithms\n3. Examine any container-specific security restrictions\n4. Try alternative authentication methods (key-based)\n\nThe core functionality - Git repository with automatic deployment to separate HTTPS endpoints - is fully operational and ready for use.\n"}
